{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>They shall be whole for you, and their drink-offerings.</b> The drink-offerings too must be whole. From here the Rabbis of blessed memory derived: one ascends with wine, meal is unfit for drink-offerings — for nothing is fit to be offered upon the altar except the choicest of its kind, and anything that has no disqualifying blemish but is merely lean or ugly is not offered ab initio. For if one were obligated to bring a burnt-offering, he may not bring a lean or ugly lamb and say, 'behold it has no blemish,' for concerning this it is said (Malachi 1:14): ״וארור נוכל ויש בעדרו זכר״ — rather, he must bring of the choicest. And so Israel would do in the time when the Temple stood: they would bring rams from Moab, lambs whose broad-tailed portion was wide from Hebron, doves from the King's Mountain, and oil from Tekoa — all was the choicest of its kind. And so we find in the offering of Hevel (Genesis 4:4): ״והבל הביא גם הוא מבכורות צאנו ומחלבהן״ — and his offering found favor; and concerning Kayin it is stated that he did not bring of the choicest (ibid.): ״ואל קין ואל מנחתו לא שעה״. And so it is written (Deuteronomy 12:11): ״וכל מבחר נדריכםם, and it is written (Numbers 18:29): ״בהרימכם את חלבו ממנו״. And even the wood of the arrangement that they would set upon the altar for the offerings — we were commanded concerning it that it be of the choicest, that there be no worm in it, and one may not bring wood from a building that was demolished, but only new wood always. And all woods are fit for the arrangement except olive-wood and vine-wood, on account of the settlement of the Land of Israel. And so we were commanded concerning the oil of the Menorah to bring of the choicest, and not all oils are fit for the Menorah but only olive oil pressed from the first pressing alone. And for this reason the Rabbis of blessed memory forbade oil into which a mouse fell to be used for kindling the synagogue lamps, and the opinion of the Geonim of blessed memory is that if it was crushed and there is in the oil sixty times its amount, it is permitted for eating, and if it was not crushed, he casts it out and the oil is permitted by a ratio of sixty against it; and even though the oil is permitted for eating, it is unfit for illumination, as it is said (Malachi 1:8): ״הקריבהו נא לפחתך״ — for we require the choicest thing."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:36:52.438868801Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}